    "**two runs of one controller overlap, and each decides on what it read while the other changes it -- so a write lands on whatever now occupies the path, and a decision counts a roster that no longer exists.** INVALID STATE: a stale writer deletes or rewrites a record that a later run created, and a stale decision acts on a count the other run has already changed. HARM: the controller's ceilings are counted twice over half the truth -- a fourth card bought under a three-card ceiling.",
